      "problem": "Simplify $2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9\\cdot 6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\cdot 3\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ (6x-5x)\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
